  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 2'-De-N-Methylaplysinopsin and the CD276 antigen, mediated through a series of targets. The drug, 2'-De-N-Methylaplysinopsin, is identified as a target of JAR, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including 5,7-Dihydroxy-6-(3-Methylbutanoyl)-8-(3-Methylbut-2-Enyl)-4-Pentylchromen-2-One and [(4aS,9S,10R,10aS)-6-acetyloxy-10-[[(4bS,8aS)-4b,8,8-trimethyl-2-propan-2-yl-5,6,7,8a-tetrahydrophenanthren-3-yl]oxy]-1,1,4a-trimethyl-7-propan-2-yl-2,3,4,9,10,10a-hexahydrophenanthren-9-yl] acetate. All of these compounds are ultimately linked to the CD276 antigen, indicating a possible pathway through which 2'-De-N-Methylaplysinopsin may exert its effects. The evidence suggests that the drug may act through a mechanism involving the targeting of JAR, which is a known target of multiple compounds, and that these compounds may have a role in modulating the CD276 antigen. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that 2'-De-N-Methylaplysinopsin may interact with the CD276 antigen through a complex network of targets, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
